<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == (\old(i == this.size() - 1) ? null : \old(this.get(i + 1)));</code>

This assert statement checks that for every valid index `i` from the insertion point to the old size of the vector, the element at `i` after the insertion is either `null` (if `i` was the last index) or equal to the element at `i + 1` before the insertion.--------------------<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == (\old(i < \old(this.size()) ? \old(this.get(i)) : null));</code>

This assert statement ensures that for every valid index `i` from the insertion point `index` to the old size of the vector, the element at `i+1` after the insertion is either `null` or equal to the element at `i` before the insertion. This captures the behavior described in the comment.--------------------<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == (\old(i == this.size() - 1) ? null : \old(this.get(i + 1)));</code>

This assertion ensures that for every valid index `i` starting from the insertion point `index` up to the old size of the vector, the element at `i` after the insertion is either `null` (if `i` was the last index) or equal to the element at `i + 1` before the insertion.--------------------